{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788807749386403191,"compiled_state":{"alias":"awake-shoddy-gyrfalcon","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"727bfba63be58bd1dd4f9860635275510cfdd076e54178cb207b5c68045d43d4","event_uuid":"b34e5477-f789-4025-b1f9-b969caa6f1b7","position":{"commit_sha":"72ec5559eb76eb7790d6adb39bec596869c5e538","position":"1788807318703641225-b34e5477-f789-4025-b1f9-b969caa6f1b7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ed4199a80e8ed0be3c9dc577a7a85efc393fdff0d1f550949270b967799edc63","event_uuid":"1183494f-cc83-4380-9d25-2d6d61abbf34","position":{"commit_sha":"46d36a17c1fdb3f29bd31fc9ebd1b3c991a82be7","position":"1788807578032455349-1183494f-cc83-4380-9d25-2d6d61abbf34"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"be69d55e4c0e42fa6ce0ab6019316a888e9b0590412dea85d9a5af957ea76d8e","event_uuid":"2c7bb1be-6206-4aa6-8bf9-9f7f658344a5","position":{"commit_sha":"87652ca546004a2a54c4b32374f564702b1a4f05","position":"1788807749386403190-2c7bb1be-6206-4aa6-8bf9-9f7f658344a5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation detail for this story (the description carries the decisions).\n\nFrom enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, the unpaired held-out paragraph:\n\nUnpaired held-out (88): 10 are handled elsewhere (8 `tests/scripts/*_seam_clean_heldout.py` + `test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py` in S1, `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py` deleted in S3); the remaining **78** are renamed to drop `_heldout` (unit 55, interfaces 18, scripts 4, integration 1). Three are cross-tier twins whose base lives in another directory and would collide on basename under pytest's prepend import mode (13 `__init__.py` files; no `--import-mode` in `pyproject.toml:8`): `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py` (base `tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py`) → `test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_baseline_normalization_heldout.py` (base in `tests/integration/…`) → `test_baseline_normalization_diffing.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_identity_264f_heldout.py` (base `tests/unit/test_identity_264f.py`) → `test_identity_264f_reconciler.py`. Do not merge across tiers.\n\n(\"S1\" and \"S3\" in that paragraph are the test-suite epic's stories E10a-S1 skaldic-paradoxal-huemul and E10a-S3 aware-obvious-sphinx.)\n\nRename mechanics:\n1. Enumerate the set at execution time, after S2, S3 and S4 have merged every pair: `git ls-files 'tests/**/test_*_heldout.py'` lists exactly the 78 files (the 10 handled elsewhere are already gone).\n2. For each file except the three cross-tier ones: `git mv tests/<dir>/test_<name>_heldout.py tests/<dir>/test_<name>.py` — the target basename does not exist anywhere under `tests/` (check with `git ls-files tests | xargs -n1 basename | sort | uniq -d` after the batch).\n3. The three cross-tier files take the `_store`, `_diffing` and `_reconciler` suffixes named above.\n4. `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass_heldout.py` → `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass.py`; it carries the tests E10a-S1 moved into it.\n5. No content change in any renamed module; the module docstrings keep their held-out \"what it proves\" paragraphs and every bug cite named in enumeration (6) (`test_sync_only_scalar_update_dispatch_heldout.py` af1b, `test_richtext_port_heldout.py` 1bb2-5da5 — merged in S2 —, `test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py` 0fad, `test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py` 7c26-4ac8-04a3-440e, `test_dc_pat_required_heldout.py` cd78, `test_dc_transition_by_status_heldout.py` 7f93, `test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py` 9263/deac, `test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py` deac, `test_identity_dc_inbound_heldout.py` 5f48, `test_identity_write_retention_heldout.py` 387d, `test_index_lag_duplicate_heldout.py` 21fc, `test_jira_key_local_id_heldout.py` 23ed, `test_retry_after_zero_guard_heldout.py` 3604-891f-e301-4aff, `test_identity_txn_signing_heldout.py` 0ba4, `test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py` beb1/ed5c, `test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py`).\n6. Record on this ticket one 78-row table: old path, new path, `pytest --collect-only -q` count before and after (equal per row).\n\nPaths under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` are stated at the current name (origin/main 083620b0); the reconciler epic (friended-brainsick-degus) rename carries them.","timestamp":1788807578032455349}],"created_at":1788807318703641225,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n88 held-out modules (17,106 LOC) have no base twin. 10 of them are handled elsewhere: the 8 `tests/scripts/*_seam_clean_heldout.py` modules and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py` in the test-suite epic's seam story (E10a-S1), and `tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py`, deleted in its single-owner story (E10a-S3). The remaining 78 (unit 55, interfaces 18, scripts 4, integration 1) keep a `_heldout` suffix that no longer distinguishes anything once S2, S3 and S4 have merged every pair. Three of the 78 are cross-tier twins whose base lives in another directory and would collide on basename under pytest's prepend import mode (13 `__init__.py` files under `tests/`; no `--import-mode` in `pyproject.toml:8`), so they take a disambiguating suffix instead. The rename rules and the three cross-tier renames are itemised in this ticket's first comment. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\n- `git mv` each of the 75 ordinary unpaired modules from `test_<name>_heldout.py` to `test_<name>.py`, in place, with no content change.\n- The three cross-tier files take disambiguating suffixes: `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py` (base `tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py`) → `test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_baseline_normalization_heldout.py` (base under `tests/integration/`) → `test_baseline_normalization_diffing.py`; `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_identity_264f_heldout.py` (base `tests/unit/test_identity_264f.py`) → `test_identity_264f_reconciler.py`. Do not merge across tiers.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass_heldout.py` carries the tests E10a-S1 moved into it along with the rename.\n- Paths under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` are stated at the current name; the reconciler epic (friended-brainsick-degus) rename carries them.\n- After this story `tests/**/test_*_heldout.py` matches nothing and `git ls-files tests | xargs -n1 basename | sort | uniq -d` is empty; the epic's first acceptance criterion is checked here.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the 78 unpaired `tests/**/test_*_heldout.py` modules (55 under `tests/unit/` including its subpackages, 18 under `tests/interfaces/`, 4 under `tests/scripts/`, 1 under `tests/integration/`), renamed in place. Out of scope: every merged pair (S1-S4), the 10 held-out modules handled by E10a-S1 and E10a-S3, module contents, every file under `src/`, and any test body change.\n\n## Testing\nPer file: `pytest --collect-only -q <old path>` before and `pytest --collect-only -q <new path>` after — counts equal (recorded on this ticket as one table of 78 rows). `git ls-files 'tests/**/test_*_heldout.py'` prints nothing; `git ls-files tests | xargs -n1 basename | sort | uniq -d` prints nothing; `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No `tests/**/test_*_heldout.py` file remains (`git ls-files 'tests/**/test_*_heldout.py'` prints nothing).\n- [ ] No duplicate basenames under `tests/` (`git ls-files tests | xargs -n1 basename | sort | uniq -d` prints nothing); the three cross-tier files carry their `_store`, `_diffing` and `_reconciler` suffixes.\n- [ ] Node counts per file are unchanged across the rename, from the before/after `pytest --collect-only -q` table recorded on this ticket (78 rows).\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` shows `new=0`.\n- [ ] `make verify` green.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_*_heldout.py","reason":"rename (drop _heldout; unpaired modules only)"},{"path":"tests/unit/**/test_*_heldout.py","reason":"rename (drop _heldout; unpaired modules only)"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/**/test_*_heldout.py","reason":"rename (drop _heldout; unpaired modules only)"},{"path":"tests/scripts/**/test_*_heldout.py","reason":"rename (drop _heldout; unpaired modules only)"},{"path":"tests/integration/**/test_*_heldout.py","reason":"rename (drop _heldout; unpaired modules only)"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py","reason":"rename to test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py (cross-tier twin)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_baseline_normalization_heldout.py","reason":"rename to test_baseline_normalization_diffing.py (cross-tier twin)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_identity_264f_heldout.py","reason":"rename to test_identity_264f_reconciler.py (cross-tier twin)"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass_heldout.py","reason":"rename to test_reconciler_last_pass.py (carries the E10a-S1-moved tests)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","6ed2-24e5-6985-4faa"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6ed2-24e5-6985-4faa","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"b721-6c6d-504e-45da","ticket_type":"story","title":"Rename the 78 unpaired held-out test modules to drop the _heldout suffix","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b34e5477-f789-4025-b1f9-b969caa6f1b7","1183494f-cc83-4380-9d25-2d6d61abbf34","2c7bb1be-6206-4aa6-8bf9-9f7f658344a5"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788807749386403191,"uuid":"bee60753-40e9-42f6-b343-d880e95cdc7b"}